# Toccata and Fugue in D minor, the opening
# Composer: Johann Sebastian Bach (1685-1750). Work: Toccata and Fugue in D minor, BWV 565, public domain.
# Arrangement: ours, for four chip voices, 2026-10-25. Notes written from the organ score (Bach-Gesellschaft
# Ausgabe, 1867; public-domain edition typeset by the Mutopia Project, piece 1780), bars 1 to 15 of the Toccata:
# the three mordent figures, the diminished seventh over the pedal D, the triplet figures, the descending triplets and
# the sixteenths over the repeated A. The octave doublings in bar 1, the drums and the closing chord are ours; where the
# organ goes below about 300 Hz the lead moves up an octave so the small speaker can play it.
# Rows: a 64th note in bars 1 to 3 (tempo 500, 60 ms), a twelfth of a beat from bar 4 (tempo 504, quarter = 84).
# Columns: lead (pulse 25%) | harmony (pulse 50%) | bass (triangle) | drums (noise). Tokens as in fox_run.tune.
vol 12 8 14 8
tempo 500
